IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cpp-core-definitions`
IMPORT `cp2-employer-deduct-and-remit`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, Part I, Division C: sections 24, 25 and 26. LAYER 1, from the text alone.
--
-- Section 24 makes an employer keep books and records and says how long. Section 25 is the inspection
-- section: who may enter, look at documents, question people and demand information, with the safeguards
-- for a dwelling-house and for information about unnamed persons. Section 26 protects a person who deducts
-- contributions and makes the Minister's receipt a discharge.
--
-- The powers of an authorized person or a judge are written as "may" BOOLEANs over the conditions the text
-- states: whether the power exists, never whether it is used. A duty on the person asked is a "must" BOOLEAN
-- over the same conditions. Every rule is constitutive.

§ `Division C -- records and inspection`

§§ `s 24 -- books and records`

-- src:669 | Books and records
-- src:670 | 24 (1) Every employer paying remuneration to an employee employed by him in pensionable employment shall keep records and books of account at his place of business or residence in Canada, or at such other place as may be designated by the Minister, in such form and containing such information as will enable any contributions payable under this Act or any contributions or other amounts that should have been deducted or paid to be determined, and where any such employer has failed to keep adequate records and books of account, the Minister may require him to keep such records and books of account as he may specify, and the employer shall thereafter keep records and books of account as so required.
@ref Act s 24(1) (src:669-670)
GIVEN relationship IS A `cp2 Employment relationship`
      `the payer pays remuneration to the payee in respect of the employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 24(1) — the employer must keep records and books of account` relationship `the payer pays remuneration to the payee in respect of the employment` MEANS
        `the payer is an employer of the payee` relationship
    AND `the payee is an employee of the payer` relationship
    AND `the payer pays remuneration to the payee in respect of the employment`
    AND (relationship's `employment is pensionable employment`)

-- Where the records may be kept: "at his place of business or residence in Canada, or at such other place as may
-- be designated by the Minister".
@ref Act s 24(1) (src:669-670)
DECLARE `cp2 Place where an employer keeps its records` IS ONE OF
    `the employer's place of business in Canada`
    `the employer's residence in Canada`
    `a place the Minister has designated`
    `any other place`

@ref Act s 24(1) (src:669-670)
GIVEN place IS A `cp2 Place where an employer keeps its records`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 24(1) — the employer may keep its records at the place` place MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `any other place` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- "where any such employer has failed to keep adequate records and books of account, the Minister may require him
-- to keep such records and books of account as he may specify, and the employer shall thereafter keep" them.
@ref Act s 24(1) (src:669-670)
GIVEN `the employer has failed to keep adequate records and books of account` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has required the employer to keep the records and books of account the Minister specified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 24(1) — the employer must keep the records and books of account that the Minister specified` `the employer has failed to keep adequate records and books of account` `the Minister has required the employer to keep the records and books of account the Minister specified` MEANS
        `the employer has failed to keep adequate records and books of account`
    AND `the Minister has required the employer to keep the records and books of account the Minister specified`

-- src:671 | Keeping of records and books of account
-- src:672 | (2) Every employer required by this section to keep records and books of account shall retain those records and books of account and every account and voucher necessary to verify the information contained therein until the expiration of six years from the end of the year in respect of which those records and books of account are kept or until written permission for their prior disposal is given by the Minister.
@ref Act s 24(2) (src:671-672)
GIVEN `the year in respect of which the records and books of account are kept` IS A NUMBER
      `the day the Minister gave written permission for their prior disposal, if the Minister has` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 24(2) — the last day the employer must retain the records and books of account` `the year in respect of which the records and books of account are kept` `the day the Minister gave written permission for their prior disposal, if the Minister has` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day the Minister gave written permission for their prior disposal, if the Minister has`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `add years` (`s 2(1) — the last day of a year` `the year in respect of which the records and books of account are kept`) 6
    WHEN JUST permission THEN
        IF permission AT MOST (`add years` (`s 2(1) — the last day of a year` `the year in respect of which the records and books of account are kept`) 6)
        THEN permission
        ELSE `add years` (`s 2(1) — the last day of a year` `the year in respect of which the records and books of account are kept`) 6

@ref Act s 24(2) (src:671-672)
GIVEN `the day in question` IS A DATE
      `the year in respect of which the records and books of account are kept` IS A NUMBER
      `the day the Minister gave written permission for their prior disposal, if the Minister has` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 24(2) — the employer must still retain the records and books of account on the day` `the day in question` `the year in respect of which the records and books of account are kept` `the day the Minister gave written permission for their prior disposal, if the Minister has` MEANS
    `the day in question` AT MOST (`s 24(2) — the last day the employer must retain the records and books of account` `the year in respect of which the records and books of account are kept` `the day the Minister gave written permission for their prior disposal, if the Minister has`)

-- src:673 | Electronic records
-- src:674 | (2.1) Every employer required by this section to keep records who does so electronically shall retain them in an electronically readable format for the retention period referred to in subsection (2).
-- src:675 | Exemption
-- src:676 | (2.2) The Minister may, on such terms and conditions as are acceptable to the Minister, exempt an employer or a class of employers from the requirement in subsection (2.1).
@ref Act s 24(2.1), (2.2) (src:673-676)
GIVEN `the Minister has exempted the employer, or a class of employers that includes it, on terms acceptable to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer meets those terms` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 24(2.2) — the employer is exempt from the requirement to retain electronic records in an electronically readable format` `the Minister has exempted the employer, or a class of employers that includes it, on terms acceptable to the Minister` `the employer meets those terms` MEANS
        `the Minister has exempted the employer, or a class of employers that includes it, on terms acceptable to the Minister`
    AND `the employer meets those terms`

@ref Act s 24(2.1) (src:673-676)
GIVEN `the employer keeps the records electronically` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer is exempt under subsection 24(2.2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 24(2.1) — the employer must retain the records in an electronically readable format for the retention period` `the employer keeps the records electronically` `the employer is exempt under subsection 24(2.2)` MEANS
        `the employer keeps the records electronically`
    AND (NOT `the employer is exempt under subsection 24(2.2)`)

-- src:677 | Retention for ruling or appeal
-- src:678 | (3) If the employer or an employee of the employer is subject to a ruling under section 26.1 or has made an appeal to the Minister under section 27 or 27.1, the employer shall retain every record, book of account, account and voucher necessary for dealing with the ruling or the appeal until the ruling is made or the appeal is disposed of and any further appeal is disposed of or the time for filing a further appeal has expired.
@ref Act s 24(3) (src:677-678)
GIVEN `the employer or an employee of the employer is subject to a ruling under section 26.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ruling has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer or an employee of the employer has made an appeal to the Minister under section 27 or 27.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal has been disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any further appeal has been disposed of or the time for filing a further appeal has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 24(3) — the employer must still retain every record, book of account, account and voucher necessary for the ruling or appeal` `the employer or an employee of the employer is subject to a ruling under section 26.1` `the ruling has been made` `the employer or an employee of the employer has made an appeal to the Minister under section 27 or 27.1` `the appeal has been disposed of` `any further appeal has been disposed of or the time for filing a further appeal has expired` MEANS
        (    `the employer or an employee of the employer is subject to a ruling under section 26.1`
         AND (NOT `the ruling has been made`))
    OR  (    `the employer or an employee of the employer has made an appeal to the Minister under section 27 or 27.1`
         AND (    (NOT `the appeal has been disposed of`)
              OR  (NOT `any further appeal has been disposed of or the time for filing a further appeal has expired`)))

§§ `s 25(1) -- the words the section defines`

-- src:679 | Interpretation
-- src:680 | 25 (1) In this section,
-- src:681 | authorized person means a person authorized by the Minister for the purposes of this section; (personne autorisée)
@ref Act s 25(1) "authorized person" (src:680-681)
GIVEN `the person has been authorized by the Minister for the purposes of section 25` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25(1) — an authorized person` `the person has been authorized by the Minister for the purposes of section 25` MEANS
    `the person has been authorized by the Minister for the purposes of section 25`

-- "documents includes money, securities and any of the following, whether computerized or not: books, records,
-- letters, telegrams, vouchers, invoices, accounts and statements (financial or otherwise)". "Includes" leaves the
-- list open (fork F4 of the keel): a thing outside the list gives NOTHING, never FALSE.
-- src:682 | documents includes money, securities and any of the following, whether computerized or not: books, records, letters, telegrams, vouchers, invoices, accounts and statements (financial or otherwise); (documents)
@ref Act s 25(1) "documents" (src:682)
DECLARE `cp2 Kind of thing that may be a document` IS ONE OF
    `money, as a document`
    `securities, as a document`
    `books, whether computerized or not`
    `records, whether computerized or not`
    `letters, whether computerized or not`
    `telegrams, whether computerized or not`
    `vouchers, whether computerized or not`
    `invoices, whether computerized or not`
    `accounts, whether computerized or not`
    `statements, financial or otherwise, whether computerized or not`
    `another kind of thing`

@ref Act s 25(1) "documents" (src:682)
GIVEN kind IS A `cp2 Kind of thing that may be a document`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25(1) — documents` kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `another kind of thing` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:683 | dwelling-house means the whole or any part of a building or structure that is kept or occupied as a permanent or temporary residence and includes
-- src:684 | (a) a building within the curtilage of a dwelling-house that is connected to it by a doorway or by a covered and enclosed passageway, and
-- src:685 | (b) a unit that is designed to be mobile and to be used as a permanent or temporary residence and that is being used as such a residence; (maison d’habitation)
@ref Act s 25(1) "dwelling-house" (src:683-685)
GIVEN `the whole or any part of a building or structure is kept or occupied as a permanent or temporary residence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a building within the curtilage of a dwelling-house that is connected to it by a doorway or by a covered and enclosed passageway` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a unit designed to be mobile and to be used as a permanent or temporary residence and it is being used as such a residence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25(1) — a dwelling-house` `the whole or any part of a building or structure is kept or occupied as a permanent or temporary residence` `it is a building within the curtilage of a dwelling-house that is connected to it by a doorway or by a covered and enclosed passageway` `it is a unit designed to be mobile and to be used as a permanent or temporary residence and it is being used as such a residence` MEANS
        `the whole or any part of a building or structure is kept or occupied as a permanent or temporary residence`
    OR  `it is a building within the curtilage of a dwelling-house that is connected to it by a doorway or by a covered and enclosed passageway`
    OR  `it is a unit designed to be mobile and to be used as a permanent or temporary residence and it is being used as such a residence`

-- src:686 | judge means a judge of a superior court having jurisdiction in the province where the matter arises or a judge of the Federal Court. (juge)
@ref Act s 25(1) "judge" (src:686)
GIVEN `the person is a judge of a superior court having jurisdiction in the province where the matter arises` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a judge of the Federal Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25(1) — a judge` `the person is a judge of a superior court having jurisdiction in the province where the matter arises` `the person is a judge of the Federal Court` MEANS
        `the person is a judge of a superior court having jurisdiction in the province where the matter arises`
    OR  `the person is a judge of the Federal Court`

§§ `s 25(2) to (4) -- inspections, and entry into a dwelling-house`

-- src:687 | Inspections
-- src:688 | (2) An authorized person may, at any reasonable time, for any purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act, inspect, audit or examine any document that relates or may relate to the information that is or should be contained in the records or books of account or to the amount of any contribution payable under this Act and, for those purposes, the authorized person may
-- src:689 | (a) subject to subsection (3), enter any premises or place where any records or books of account are or should be kept; and
-- src:690 | (b) require the owner, occupant or person in charge of the premises or place to give to the authorized person all reasonable assistance and to answer all proper questions relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act and, for that purpose, require the owner, occupant or person in charge of the premises or place to attend at such premises or place with the authorized person.
@ref Act s 25(2) (src:687-690)
GIVEN `the person is an authorized person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time is a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose relates to the administration or enforcement of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document relates or may relate to the information that is or should be contained in the records or books of account, or to the amount of any contribution payable under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25(2) — the authorized person may inspect, audit or examine the document` `the person is an authorized person` `the time is a reasonable time` `the purpose relates to the administration or enforcement of this Act` `the document relates or may relate to the information that is or should be contained in the records or books of account, or to the amount of any contribution payable under this Act` MEANS
        `the person is an authorized person`
    AND `the time is a reasonable time`
    AND `the purpose relates to the administration or enforcement of this Act`
    AND `the document relates or may relate to the information that is or should be contained in the records or books of account, or to the amount of any contribution payable under this Act`

-- src:691 | Warrant required to enter dwelling-house
-- src:692 | (3) Where a premises or place referred to in subsection (2) is a dwelling-house, an authorized person may not enter that dwelling-house without the consent of the occupant except under the authority of a warrant issued under subsection (4).
@ref Act s 25(3) (src:691-692)
GIVEN `the premises or place is a dwelling-house` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the occupant consents to the entry` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entry is under the authority of a warrant issued under subsection 25(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25(3) — the authorized person may enter the premises or place` `the premises or place is a dwelling-house` `the occupant consents to the entry` `the entry is under the authority of a warrant issued under subsection 25(4)` MEANS
        (NOT `the premises or place is a dwelling-house`)
    OR  `the occupant consents to the entry`
    OR  `the entry is under the authority of a warrant issued under subsection 25(4)`

@ref Act s 25(2)(a) (src:687-690)
GIVEN `the person is an authorized person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time is a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose relates to the administration or enforcement of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `records or books of account are or should be kept at the premises or place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the premises or place is a dwelling-house` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the occupant consents to the entry` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entry is under the authority of a warrant issued under subsection 25(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25(2)(a) — the authorized person may enter the premises or place` `the person is an authorized person` `the time is a reasonable time` `the purpose relates to the administration or enforcement of this Act` `records or books of account are or should be kept at the premises or place` `the premises or place is a dwelling-house` `the occupant consents to the entry` `the entry is under the authority of a warrant issued under subsection 25(4)` MEANS
        `the person is an authorized person`
    AND `the time is a reasonable time`
    AND `the purpose relates to the administration or enforcement of this Act`
    AND `records or books of account are or should be kept at the premises or place`
    AND `s 25(3) — the authorized person may enter the premises or place` `the premises or place is a dwelling-house` `the occupant consents to the entry` `the entry is under the authority of a warrant issued under subsection 25(4)`

@ref Act s 25(2)(b) (src:687-690)
GIVEN `the person is an authorized person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time is a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose relates to the administration or enforcement of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person asked is the owner, occupant or person in charge of the premises or place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25(2)(b) — the owner, occupant or person in charge must give all reasonable assistance, answer all proper questions and attend` `the person is an authorized person` `the time is a reasonable time` `the purpose relates to the administration or enforcement of this Act` `the person asked is the owner, occupant or person in charge of the premises or place` MEANS
        `the person is an authorized person`
    AND `the time is a reasonable time`
    AND `the purpose relates to the administration or enforcement of this Act`
    AND `the person asked is the owner, occupant or person in charge of the premises or place`

-- Subsection (4) has two outcomes for an ex parte application by the Minister to a judge. If the judge is satisfied
-- by information on oath of (a), (b) and (c), the judge "shall issue a warrant". If the judge is not satisfied that
-- entry is necessary, the judge "shall" order the occupant to give access to documents (d) and make any other
-- appropriate order (e), to the extent that access has been or may be expected to be refused and the document is or
-- may be expected to be kept in the dwelling-house. A case in neither (for example (b) satisfied but (c) not) is not
-- decided by the text: the rule says so with a constructor, never FALSE.
-- src:693 | Warrant or order
-- src:694 | (4) Where, on ex parte application by the Minister, a judge is satisfied by information on oath
-- src:695 | (a) that there are reasonable grounds to believe that a dwelling-house is a premises or place referred to in subsection (2),
-- src:696 | (b) that entry into the dwelling-house is necessary for any purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act, and
-- src:697 | (c) that entry into the dwelling-house has been refused or that there are reasonable grounds for believing that entry thereto will be refused,
-- src:698 | the judge shall issue a warrant authorizing an authorized person to enter that dwelling-house subject to such conditions as may be specified in the warrant but, where the judge is not satisfied that entry into that dwelling-house is necessary for any purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act, the judge shall
-- src:699 | (d) order the occupant of the dwelling-house to provide an authorized person with reasonable access to any document that is or should be kept therein, and
-- src:700 | (e) make such other order as is appropriate in the circumstances to carry out the purposes of this Act
-- src:701 | to the extent that access has been or may be expected to be refused and that the document is or may be expected to be kept in the dwelling-house.
@ref Act s 25(4) (src:693-701)
DECLARE `cp2 Outcome of the Minister's application about a dwelling-house` IS ONE OF
    `the judge must issue a warrant authorizing an authorized person to enter the dwelling-house`
    `the judge must order the occupant to give an authorized person reasonable access to the documents, and make any other appropriate order`
    `the text does not say what the judge must do on the application`

@ref Act s 25(4) (src:693-701)
GIVEN `the application is made ex parte by the Minister to a judge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the dwelling-house is a premises or place referred to in subsection 25(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that entry into the dwelling-house is necessary for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that entry has been refused or that there are reasonable grounds for believing that it will be refused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `access to the document has been or may be expected to be refused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is or may be expected to be kept in the dwelling-house` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `cp2 Outcome of the Minister's application about a dwelling-house`
`s 25(4) — what the judge must do on the Minister's application` `the application is made ex parte by the Minister to a judge` `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the dwelling-house is a premises or place referred to in subsection 25(2)` `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that entry into the dwelling-house is necessary for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act` `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that entry has been refused or that there are reasonable grounds for believing that it will be refused` `access to the document has been or may be expected to be refused` `the document is or may be expected to be kept in the dwelling-house` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the application is made ex parte by the Minister to a judge`) THEN `the text does not say what the judge must do on the application`
        IF `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the dwelling-house is a premises or place referred to in subsection 25(2)` AND `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that entry into the dwelling-house is necessary for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act` AND `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that entry has been refused or that there are reasonable grounds for believing that it will be refused` THEN `the judge must issue a warrant authorizing an authorized person to enter the dwelling-house`
        IF (NOT `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that entry into the dwelling-house is necessary for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act`) AND `access to the document has been or may be expected to be refused` AND `the document is or may be expected to be kept in the dwelling-house` THEN `the judge must order the occupant to give an authorized person reasonable access to the documents, and make any other appropriate order`
        OTHERWISE `the text does not say what the judge must do on the application`

§§ `s 25(5) to (11) -- requirements to provide information or documents`

-- src:702 | Requirement to provide documents or information
-- src:703 | (5) Notwithstanding any other provision of this Act, the Minister may, subject to subsection (6), for any purpose related to the administration or enforcement of this Act, by notice served personally or by registered or certified mail, require that any person provide, within such reasonable time as is stipulated in the notice,
-- src:704 | (a) any information or additional information, including a return of income or a supplementary return; or
-- src:705 | (b) any document.
@ref Act s 25(5) (src:702-705)
GIVEN `the purpose relates to the administration or enforcement of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice was served personally` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice was served by registered or certified mail` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice stipulates a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is permitted to impose the requirement under subsection 25(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25(5) — the person must provide the information or document the notice requires` `the purpose relates to the administration or enforcement of this Act` `the notice was served personally` `the notice was served by registered or certified mail` `the notice stipulates a reasonable time` `the Minister is permitted to impose the requirement under subsection 25(6)` MEANS
        `the purpose relates to the administration or enforcement of this Act`
    AND (`the notice was served personally` OR `the notice was served by registered or certified mail`)
    AND `the notice stipulates a reasonable time`
    AND `the Minister is permitted to impose the requirement under subsection 25(6)`

-- src:706 | Unnamed persons
-- src:707 | (6) The Minister shall not impose on any person, in this section referred to as a “third party”, a requirement under subsection (5) to provide information or any document relating to one or more unnamed persons unless the Minister first obtains the authorization of a judge under subsection (7).
@ref Act s 25(6) (src:706-707)
GIVEN `the requirement relates to one or more unnamed persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has first obtained the authorization of a judge under subsection 25(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25(6) — the Minister may impose the requirement on the third party` `the requirement relates to one or more unnamed persons` `the Minister has first obtained the authorization of a judge under subsection 25(7)` MEANS
        (NOT `the requirement relates to one or more unnamed persons`)
    OR  `the Minister has first obtained the authorization of a judge under subsection 25(7)`

-- src:708 | Judicial authorization
-- src:709 | (7) On ex parte application by the Minister, a judge may, subject to such conditions as the judge considers appropriate, authorize the Minister to impose on a third party a requirement under subsection (5) relating to an unnamed person or more than one unnamed person, in this section referred to as the “group”, where the judge is satisfied by information on oath that
-- src:710 | (a) the person or group is ascertainable; and
-- src:711 | (b) the requirement is made to verify compliance by the person or persons in the group with any duty or obligation under this Act.
-- src:712 | (c) and (d) [Repealed, 1998, c. 19, s. 254]
@ref Act s 25(7) (src:708-711)
GIVEN `the application is made ex parte by the Minister to a judge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that the person or group is ascertainable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that the requirement is made to verify compliance by the person or persons in the group with any duty or obligation under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25(7) — the judge may authorize the Minister to impose the requirement relating to unnamed persons` `the application is made ex parte by the Minister to a judge` `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that the person or group is ascertainable` `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that the requirement is made to verify compliance by the person or persons in the group with any duty or obligation under this Act` MEANS
        `the application is made ex parte by the Minister to a judge`
    AND `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that the person or group is ascertainable`
    AND `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that the requirement is made to verify compliance by the person or persons in the group with any duty or obligation under this Act`

-- src:713 | Service of authorization
-- src:714 | (8) Where an authorization is granted under subsection (7), the authorization shall be served together with the notice referred to in subsection (5).
@ref Act s 25(8) (src:713-714)
GIVEN `an authorization has been granted under subsection 25(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorization was served together with the notice referred to in subsection 25(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25(8) — the authorization has been served as required` `an authorization has been granted under subsection 25(7)` `the authorization was served together with the notice referred to in subsection 25(5)` MEANS
        (NOT `an authorization has been granted under subsection 25(7)`)
    OR  `the authorization was served together with the notice referred to in subsection 25(5)`

-- src:715 | Review of authorization
-- src:716 | (9) Where an authorization is granted under subsection (7), a third party on whom a notice is served under subsection (5) may, within 15 days after the service of the notice, apply to the judge who granted the authorization or, where the judge is unable to act, to another judge of the same court for a review of the authorization.
@ref Act s 25(9) (src:715-716)
GIVEN `an authorization has been granted under subsection 25(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a third party on whom a notice has been served under subsection 25(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the notice was served` IS A DATE
      `the day of the application for review` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25(9) — the third party may apply for a review of the authorization` `an authorization has been granted under subsection 25(7)` `the person is a third party on whom a notice has been served under subsection 25(5)` `the day the notice was served` `the day of the application for review` MEANS
        `an authorization has been granted under subsection 25(7)`
    AND `the person is a third party on whom a notice has been served under subsection 25(5)`
    AND `a date is within a time limit after a start date`
            `the day of the application for review`
            `the day the notice was served`
            (`a number of days` WITH `number of days` IS 15)

-- src:717 | Powers on review
-- src:718 | (10) On hearing an application under subsection (9), a judge may cancel the authorization previously granted if the judge is not then satisfied that the conditions in paragraphs (7)(a) and (b) have been met and the judge may confirm or vary the authorization if satisfied that those conditions have been met.
@ref Act s 25(10) (src:717-718)
DECLARE `cp2 Outcome of a review of an authorization` IS ONE OF
    `the judge may cancel the authorization`
    `the judge may confirm or vary the authorization`

@ref Act s 25(10) (src:717-718)
GIVEN `the judge is satisfied that the conditions in paragraphs 25(7)(a) and (b) have been met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `cp2 Outcome of a review of an authorization`
`s 25(10) — what the judge may do on the review` `the judge is satisfied that the conditions in paragraphs 25(7)(a) and (b) have been met` MEANS
    IF `the judge is satisfied that the conditions in paragraphs 25(7)(a) and (b) have been met`
    THEN `the judge may confirm or vary the authorization`
    ELSE `the judge may cancel the authorization`

-- src:719 | Additional remedy
-- src:720 | (11) Where a person is found guilty of an offence under subsection 41(2) for failing to comply with a requirement under subsection (5), the court may make such order as it deems proper in order to enforce compliance with the requirement.
@ref Act s 25(11) (src:719-720)
GIVEN `the person has been found guilty of an offence under subsection 41(2) for failing to comply with a requirement under subsection 25(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25(11) — the court may make such order as it deems proper to enforce compliance with the requirement` `the person has been found guilty of an offence under subsection 41(2) for failing to comply with a requirement under subsection 25(5)` MEANS
    `the person has been found guilty of an offence under subsection 41(2) for failing to comply with a requirement under subsection 25(5)`

§§ `s 25(12) and (13) -- copies as evidence, and compliance`

-- src:721 | Copies as evidence
-- src:722 | (12) Where any document is inspected, audited, examined or provided under this section, the person by whom it is inspected, audited or examined or to whom it is provided or any officer of the Canada Revenue Agency may make, or cause to be made, one or more copies thereof and, in the case of an electronic document, make or cause to be made a print-out of the electronic document, and any document purporting to be certified by the Minister or an authorized person to be a copy of the document, or to be a print-out of an electronic document, made pursuant to this subsection is evidence of the nature and content of the original document and has the same probative force as the original document would have if it were proven in the ordinary way.
@ref Act s 25(12) (src:721-722)
GIVEN `the document has been inspected, audited, examined or provided under section 25` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the maker is the person by whom it was inspected, audited or examined, the person to whom it was provided, or an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25(12) — a copy or print-out of the document may be made` `the document has been inspected, audited, examined or provided under section 25` `the maker is the person by whom it was inspected, audited or examined, the person to whom it was provided, or an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency` MEANS
        `the document has been inspected, audited, examined or provided under section 25`
    AND `the maker is the person by whom it was inspected, audited or examined, the person to whom it was provided, or an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency`

@ref Act s 25(12) (src:721-722)
GIVEN `the document purports to be certified by the Minister or an authorized person to be a copy, or a print-out of an electronic document, made under subsection 25(12)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25(12) — the certified copy is evidence of the nature and content of the original with the same probative force` `the document purports to be certified by the Minister or an authorized person to be a copy, or a print-out of an electronic document, made under subsection 25(12)` MEANS
    `the document purports to be certified by the Minister or an authorized person to be a copy, or a print-out of an electronic document, made under subsection 25(12)`

-- src:723 | Compliance
-- src:724 | (13) No person shall hinder, molest or interfere with any person doing anything that he is authorized to do by or pursuant to this section or prevent or attempt to prevent any person from doing any such thing and, notwithstanding any other Act or law, every person shall, unless he is unable to do so, do everything he is required to do by or pursuant to this section.
@ref Act s 25(13) (src:723-724)
GIVEN `the person hindered, molested or interfered with a person doing anything the person is authorized to do under section 25, or prevented or attempted to prevent a person from doing it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25(13) — the person contravenes the prohibition on hindering a person acting under section 25` `the person hindered, molested or interfered with a person doing anything the person is authorized to do under section 25, or prevented or attempted to prevent a person from doing it` MEANS
    `the person hindered, molested or interfered with a person doing anything the person is authorized to do under section 25, or prevented or attempted to prevent a person from doing it`

@ref Act s 25(13) (src:723-724)
GIVEN `the person did everything the person is required to do by or under section 25` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was unable to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25(13) — the person fails to do everything required under section 25` `the person did everything the person is required to do by or under section 25` `the person was unable to do so` MEANS
        (NOT `the person did everything the person is required to do by or under section 25`)
    AND (NOT `the person was unable to do so`)

§§ `s 26 -- the person who deducts, and the Minister's receipt`

-- src:725 | No action against person deducting
-- src:726 | 26 (1) No action lies against any person for deducting any sum of money in compliance or intended compliance with this Act.
@ref Act s 26(1) (src:725-726)
GIVEN `the person deducted a sum of money` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deduction was in compliance or intended compliance with this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 26(1) — no action lies against the person for the deduction` `the person deducted a sum of money` `the deduction was in compliance or intended compliance with this Act` MEANS
        `the person deducted a sum of money`
    AND `the deduction was in compliance or intended compliance with this Act`

-- src:727 | Receipt of Minister sufficient discharge
-- src:728 | (2) The receipt of the Minister for an amount deducted by any person as required by or under this Act is a good and sufficient discharge of the liability of any debtor to his creditor with respect thereto to the extent of the amount referred to in the receipt.
@ref Act s 26(2) (src:727-728)
GIVEN `the Minister's receipt is for an amount deducted by a person as required by or under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount referred to in the receipt` IS A NUMBER
      `the debtor's liability to the creditor with respect to the amount deducted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 26(2) — the extent to which the Minister's receipt discharges the debtor's liability to the creditor` `the Minister's receipt is for an amount deducted by a person as required by or under this Act` `the amount referred to in the receipt` `the debtor's liability to the creditor with respect to the amount deducted` MEANS
    IF `the Minister's receipt is for an amount deducted by a person as required by or under this Act`
    THEN min `the amount referred to in the receipt` `the debtor's liability to the creditor with respect to the amount deducted`
    ELSE 0
